{#
    One navigation list, wherever it is being drawn.

    The rail draws it twice — the main group and the tools group — and the
    narrow screen's drawer draws it once more. All three are the same markup
    over lists `NavigationService` has already decided, so a change to how a
    navigation item looks is one edit rather than three that drift.

    `links`  the list of NavLink to draw

    A list and not a landmark: whoever includes this owns the `<nav>` around it,
    because the drawer's list sits inside the bottom bar's own and nesting one
    navigation landmark in another tells a screen reader there are two.

    The icon is an empty span the bundle fills in: see `assets/js/icons.js`. It
    carries `aria-hidden`, because what says where the link goes is the text
    beside it — which is also why a browser with the script blocked loses
    nothing but the picture.
#}
<ul class="nav-list">
    {% for link in links %}
        <li>
            <a class="nav-link{{ link.active ? ' is-active' : '' }}"
               href="{{ link.href }}"
               {{ link.active ? 'aria-current="page"' : '' }}>
                <span class="nav-icon" data-icon="{{ link.icon }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="nav-label">{{ t(link.labelKey) }}</span>
            </a>
        </li>
    {% endfor %}
</ul>
